{
  "assessment": "The source provides a microscopic theory for nuclear spin thermodynamics in systems with long electron spin correlation times, including explicit equations for the inverse nuclear spin temperature and the electron-induced nuclear spin-lattice relaxation rate. The paper reports quantitative dependences on external magnetic field and electron correlation time, with parameters such as the local field and number of nuclear spins. The extracted cluster focuses on the inverse nuclear spin temperature as a function of magnetic field for two regimes of correlation time (short and long), supported by the general formula and the long-correlation-time limit. The source supports a numeric control (magnetic field), a numeric readout (inverse nuclear spin temperature), and a quantitative mechanism with parameters. However, the source does not provide explicit numeric values for the parameters (e.g., B_L, T_2e*, gamma_N) or a specific numeric domain for the magnetic field; the figures are referenced but not numerically described. Therefore, case_authoring_ready is set to false because the extracted evidence cannot support a fully quantitative interactive experiment without additional numeric data.",
