    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2406.08296v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper presents a microscopic theory of dynamic nuclear spin polarization and relaxation in systems with strongly localized electrons, bridging the spin temperature approach and the central spin model. It derives expressions for the inverse nuclear spin temperature and the electron-induced nuclear spin-lattice relaxation rate as functions of external magnetic field and electron correlation time, and discusses implications for experiments on optical cooling of nuclear spins.",
